tually did their jobs on behalf of the  public and did everything they can to  get people around the table and resolve  these disputes but there will be a lot  of people who are really worried about  the care they might get in hospitals  this winter because of strikes should  unions hold off strike action until a  time when the NHS is under less pressure  than it is right now  I think both both the unions and the  government will need to continue uh  dialogue as much as they possibly can  both in respect of trying to avoid the  strikes if possible and to minimize the  disruption that takes place that and and  I have to say that is what uh in in  respect of the health care sector that's  what Unison have been trying to do it's  been the secretaries of State for health  that haven't been engaging around the  negotiating table that's where the fault  lies for not actually seeking to find a  resolution to these matters but there's  still time it's often the case that you  can get a deal in these things at the  11th hour and that's what ministers  should be trying to do now
 

